+"""Pipeline 1 · Create raw events data -> data/bronze, from personas.
+
+Every customer is one of eight personas, a type of bank customer whose characteristics drive everything they do:
+the profile (age, income, tenure, plan, devices), the hours and days they are active, how often they use the app,
+which products interest them (with seasons: savings in January, mortgages in spring, cards before Christmas), how
+they respond to each channel and to which kind of message (offers, information, aspiration), and how likely they
+are to convert, churn and unsubscribe. Some have a life event: a young family needs a mortgage this year. Each
+customer varies around their persona.
+
+The bank behaves like a bank: email campaigns every three weeks on a Tuesday or Thursday to everyone still
+subscribed, push campaigns to app users, advice calls on weekdays in office hours to wealthier and older
+customers, banners only inside app sessions. Customers react at their own hours: an email is opened at their next
+active moment or not at all, less often after many contacts that week; a click leads to pages on its topic, maybe
+an application, an approval (mortgages and cards depend on income), a contract and an account; some contracts end
+later; irrelevant emails lead to unsubscribing. Amounts follow the product: mortgages 3–5.5× yearly income over
+20–30 years, card limits up to €15,000, deposits scaled to income.
 
 Written the way three source systems would export it, each in its own format:
   bronze/crm_contacts.csv     contacts and reactions: ISO times with Z, raw codes (EMAIL_SENT, CALL_CONNECTED, ...),
